S635 Rational Shadow Carrier
============================

Correction
----------
The usable theorem is not 'exactly one of pi+e and pi*e is rational'.
It is stronger in one direction and weaker in another: pi+e and pi*e cannot both be algebraic; therefore at least one is transcendental and hence irrational.  Which one, or whether both are transcendental, is not known.

Algebraic carrier lemma
-----------------------
For any field K, if S=x+y and P=xy both lie in K, then x and y are roots of T^2 - S*T + P in K[T].
So the pair (x,y) has descended to a quadratic carrier over K.  Contraposition: if a hidden coordinate is known transcendental over K, then the two shadows S and P cannot both be K-algebraic/tame.
With K=Qbar and (x,y)=(e,pi), both shadows algebraic would force e and pi algebraic over Qbar and hence algebraic over Q, contradicting transcendence.

Finite-field microscope
-----------------------
Unordered pairs in F_p show the same carrier geometry without analysis:
sum alone and product alone have fibers, but the joint (sum, product) shadow is injective because it is exactly the monic quadratic.

